# Copy to .env and adjust. Everything is optional on a default Steam macOS install.

# Game location.
# ADOFAI_DIR="$HOME/Library/Application Support/Steam/steamapps/common/A Dance of Fire and Ice"
# ADOFAI_MODS_DIR="$ADOFAI_DIR/Mods"

# TUFReplay.dll to compile against. Defaults to the sibling TUFReplay repository's build output
# (../TUFReplay/TUFReplay/bin/Debug/TUFReplay.dll).
# TUFREPLAY_DLL="/path/to/TUFReplay.dll"

# Where packaged mods download FFmpeg from at runtime (baked into ffmpeg-manifest.json).
# TUFREPLAY_FFMPEG_RELEASE_BASE_URL="https://github.com/kkorenn/TUFReplay-Renderer/releases/download/ffmpeg-n8.1"

# Optional FFmpeg shared library source directories (used by `install` bundling and to build the
# ffmpeg-<rid>.zip release assets).
# Point these at directories containing an FFmpeg 8 build (libavcodec.62 / avcodec-62 and friends).
# Produce LGPL-clean ones with ./scripts/run.sh prepare-lgpl-ffmpeg. When unset, `package` prepares and
# bundles the LGPL set from build/lgpl-ffmpeg automatically; `install` falls back to whatever FFmpeg is already on the machine (including
# ADOFAIRenderer's UserLibs install).
# TUFREPLAY_FFMPEG_OSX_DIR="$ADOFAI_DIR/UserLibs"
# TUFREPLAY_FFMPEG_WIN_X64_DIR="/path/to/ffmpeg-8-win64/bin"
# TUFREPLAY_FFMPEG_LINUX_X64_DIR="/path/to/ffmpeg-8-linux64/lib"
